OSF does provide a reference page for table(2).  However, it is in the
System Programmer's Reference Volume 1, which you may or may not get.  This
book contains a number of Mach functions and other "System Programming"
interfaces.  It is up to our licensees as to whether they support these
interfaces and provide the documentation.  (Volume 1 of the Sys Prog Ref
can be redistributed to non-source licensees.  Volume 2 is limited to
source licensees only).

If you do get this book on your distribution, the table.2 ref page still
may or may not be installed in man.  OSF ships documentation to its
licensees using a single source-multiple object scheme in which the
reference page source is actually located in the documentation directories
for the books.  There is a configurable file (osf1.dirlist) which
determines at installation time the documentation directories that will
provide the source for the man files.  At OSF/1 release 1.1 and 1.2, the
OSF Release Notes section 4.6 describes the process in detail.
--


