Gnu tar is the best way to do this; however, you can also:

Dump /usr to dumphost:
tar cvf - /usr | rsh dumphost "dd of=/dev/nrst1 bs=20b"

Restore /usr from dumphost:
rsh dumphost "dd if=/dev/nrst1 ibs=20b" | tar xvBpf -

